Text:
fearlessOnClick is a program that the desk runs to open files: fearlessOnClick sends a Message for each file with fearlessMessage.

Define fearlessOnClick:
A The desk opens the file x with fearlessOnClick, and x is a .fearless file.
B fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage Register b, for b the Base16 of the path of x.
C fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage Show.

Define fearlessOnClick:
A The desk opens the file x with fearlessOnClick, and x is not a .fearless file.
B fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage OpenWithOrShortcut b, for b the Base16 of the path of x.

Define fearlessOnClick:
A fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage m.
B fearlessMessage prints the Answer Refused, with the Error e.
C fearlessOnClick shows e in a dialog.

Define fearlessOnClick:
A fearlessOnClick runs fearlessMessage m.
B fearlessMessage prints e on its standard error, and ends with an error.
C fearlessOnClick shows e in a dialog.

Implementation notes:
fearlessManager passes the path of fearlessOnClick as the command of Reconciliator.reconcile: the desk opens the files of the extensions that the manager holds with fearlessOnClick.
On macOS the desk hands the files to open to fearlessOnClick in an open event; on the other desks the desk runs fearlessOnClick with the path of each file as an argument.
